**Goal** — Add `interactionBridge` and `maxInteractionTurns` to `CallContext` and `BuildHopCallbackContext`, and thread both fields into the `kind:"run"` dispatch path so `RunOperation`s can support interactive Q&A sessions.

**Motivation** — The `CallContext`, `call.ts`, and `build-hop-callback.ts` have zero references to `interactionBridge`, so any `RunOperation` that needs interactive Q&A (e.g. plan's mid-session clarification) cannot use the `callOp` dispatch path without losing that capability.

**Approach**

Extend `CallContext` in `src/operations/types.ts`:
```typescript
export interface CallContext {
  // ... existing fields ...
  readonly interactionBridge?: {
    detectQuestion: (text: string) => Promise<boolean>;
    onQuestionDetected: (text: string) => Promise<string>;
  };
  readonly maxInteractionTurns?: number;
}
```

Extend `BuildHopCallbackContext` in `src/operations/build-hop-callback.ts`:
```typescript
export interface BuildHopCallbackContext {
  // ... existing fields ...
  interactionBridge?: {
    detectQuestion: (text: string) => Promise<boolean>;
    onQuestionDetected: (text: string) => Promise<string>;
  };
  maxInteractionTurns?: number;
}
```

In `call.ts`, when assembling `runOptions` for `kind:"run"` ops, conditionally spread `interactionBridge` and `maxInteractionTurns` from `ctx` (no undefined spreading — use `...(ctx.interactionBridge ? { interactionBridge: ctx.interactionBridge } : {})` pattern). Also add both fields to `hopCtx` so they propagate into `BuildHopCallbackContext`.

In `build-hop-callback.ts`, inside the `send` closure that calls `agentManager.runAsSession(...)`, import and call `buildRunInteractionHandler` from `src/agents/acp/adapter-output` (or the re-export at `src/agents/acp/adapter` — check which path is used) to produce a non-null `interactionHandler` when `ctx.interactionBridge` is set. Pass both `interactionHandler` and `maxTurns: ctx.maxInteractionTurns` in the `RunAsSessionOpts`. The `buildRunInteractionHandler` function reads `interactionBridge`, `contextToolRuntime`, and `contextPullTools` from an `AgentRunOptions`-shaped object — all three are available in the `buildHopCallback` closure.

**Scope**
In: `src/operations/types.ts`, `src/operations/call.ts`, `src/operations/build-hop-callback.ts`.
Out: No changes to `src/agents/`, `src/runtime/`, or any pipeline stages.

**Goal** — Add `PlanPromptBuilder.jsonRepair()` static method and replace `planOp` (kind:"complete") with `planInteractiveOp` (kind:"run") in `src/operations/plan.ts`, using `hopBody` + `op.retry` for same-session JSON parse repair.

**Motivation** — When the agent produces invalid JSON for the PRD, `validatePlanOutput()` throws and the entire plan fails. There is no in-session repair — the user has to restart from scratch. The semantic/adversarial review ops already handle this with `makeParseRetryStrategy` + `sendWithParseRetry`; plan should use the same pattern.

**Approach — PlanPromptBuilder.jsonRepair()**

Add a static method to `PlanPromptBuilder` in `src/prompts/builders/plan-builder.ts`:
```typescript
static jsonRepair(attempt: number, parseError: string): string
```
Returns a repair prompt that: (a) tells the agent its previous response was not valid JSON, (b) includes the `parseError` string so the agent can see what failed, (c) instructs the agent to re-write the complete PRD JSON to `outputPath`. Biome's `noStaticOnlyClass` rule is satisfied because `build()` is already an instance method.

**Approach — PlanInteractiveInput and planInteractiveOp**

New input type:
```typescript
export interface PlanInteractiveInput {
  specContent: string;
  codebaseContext: string;
  featureName: string;
  branchName: string;
  outputPath: string;       // file path agent writes PRD to
  packages?: string[];
  packageDetails?: PackageSummary[];
  projectProfile?: ProjectProfile;
}
```

New operation (replaces `planOp`):
```typescript
export const planInteractiveOp: RunOperation<PlanInteractiveInput, PRD, PlanConfig> = {
  kind: "run",
  name: "plan-interactive",
  stage: "plan",
  session: { role: "plan", lifetime: "fresh" },
  config: planConfigSelector,
  model: (_input, ctx) => ctx.config.plan.model,
  timeoutMs: (_input, ctx) => (ctx.config.plan.timeoutSeconds ?? 600) * 1000,
  retry: makeParseRetryStrategy({
    validate: (parsed) => /* lightweight PRD shape check */,
    reviewerKind: "plan",
    maxAttempts: 3,
    prompts: {
      invalid: () => PlanPromptBuilder.jsonRepair(0, "Invalid JSON — response was not parseable"),
      truncated: () => PlanPromptBuilder.jsonRepair(0, "JSON appears truncated — please rewrite completely"),
    },
    // exhaustedFallback omitted — Bun has no synchronous file-read API;
    // disk fallback on retry exhaustion is handled at plan.ts level
  }),
  hopBody: async (initialPrompt, ctx) => {
    return ctx.sendWithParseRetry(initialPrompt);
  },
  build(input, _ctx) {
    const { taskContext, outputFormat } = new PlanPromptBuilder().build(
      input.specContent,
      input.codebaseContext,
      input.outputPath,       // outputPath variant — agent writes to file
      input.packages,
      input.packageDetails,
      input.projectProfile,
    );
    return {
      role: { id: "role", content: "", overridable: false },
      task: { id: "task", content: `${taskContext}\n\n${outputFormat}`, overridable: false },
    };
  },
  parse(output, input, _ctx) {
    return validatePlanOutput(output, input.featureName, input.branchName);
  },
  verify: async (parsed, _input, _ctx) => {
    // Return null when userStories is empty — signals recover should try disk
    if (!parsed.userStories || parsed.userStories.length === 0) return null;
    return parsed;
  },
  recover: async (input, ctx) => {
    const content = await ctx.readFile(input.outputPath);
    if (!content) return null;
    try {
      return validatePlanOutput(content, input.featureName, input.branchName);
    } catch {
      return null;
    }
  },
};
```

`planOp` (kind:"complete") and its export from `src/operations/index.ts` are removed in this story. `PlanOpInput` type export is also removed.

**Scope**
In: `src/prompts/builders/plan-builder.ts`, `src/operations/plan.ts`, `src/operations/index.ts`.
Out: No changes to `src/cli/plan.ts` (US-003).

**Goal** — Refactor `src/cli/plan.ts` to replace the `runInteractivePlan()` inner function and `--auto` branch with a single `callOp(ctx, planInteractiveOp, input)` call, threading `interactionBridge` and `maxInteractionTurns` through `CallContext`.

**Motivation** — The interactive plan path bypasses `callOp` entirely, calling `agentManager.runAs()` directly and skipping all middleware: hop-level retry, `op.verify`/`op.recover`, abort propagation, and future op-level instrumentation. The `--auto` path is a separate implementation of the same behavior.

**Approach**

Remove from `src/cli/plan.ts`:
- `auto?: boolean` from `PlanCommandOptions`
- The `} else if (options.auto) {` branch (lines 173–214)
- The `runInteractivePlan()` inner function (lines 220–301)
- The `rawResponse` variable and the final `validatePlanOutput(rawResponse, ...)` call (line 305)
- `import { planOp }` → replace with `import { planInteractiveOp }`

Add in `src/cli/plan.ts` (non-debate path):
```typescript
// Resolve interaction bridge (same logic previously inside runInteractivePlan)
const headless = !process.stdin.isTTY;
const interactionChain = config ? await _planDeps.initInteractionChain(config, headless) : null;
const configuredBridge = interactionChain
  ? buildInteractionBridge(interactionChain, { featureName: options.feature, stage: "pre-flight" })
  : undefined;
const interactionBridge = configuredBridge ?? _planDeps.createInteractionBridge();

const rt = createPlanRuntime(config, workdir, options.feature);
try {
  const prd = await callOp(
    {
      runtime: rt,
      packageView: rt.packages.resolve(),
      packageDir: workdir,
      agentName: rt.agentManager.getDefault(),
      featureName: options.feature,
      interactionBridge,
      maxInteractionTurns: config?.agent?.maxInteractionTurns,
    },
    planInteractiveOp,
    {
      specContent,
      codebaseContext,
      featureName: options.feature,
      branchName,
      outputPath,
      packages: relativePackages,
      packageDetails,
      projectProfile: config?.project,
    },
  );
  await _planDeps.writeFile(outputPath, JSON.stringify({ ...prd, project: projectName }, null, 2));
  logger?.info("plan", "[OK] PRD written", { outputPath });
  return outputPath;
} catch (err) {
  // Disk fallback: agent may have written a valid PRD even if session failed
  if (_planDeps.existsSync(outputPath)) {
    logger?.warn("plan", "callOp failed; using PRD written by agent", { outputPath });
    return outputPath;
  }
  throw err;
} finally {
  if (interactionChain) await interactionChain.destroy().catch(() => {});
  await rt.close().catch(() => {});
}
```

Debate fallback: Replace `rawResponse = await runInteractivePlan()` with a `callOp(ctx, planInteractiveOp, input)` call using the `debateRt` runtime (already created), same `interactionBridge`/`maxInteractionTurns` threading.

**`src/operations/index.ts` barrel update:**
- Remove: `export { planOp } from "./plan"` and `export type { PlanOpInput } from "./plan"`
- Add: `export { planInteractiveOp } from "./plan"` and `export type { PlanInteractiveInput } from "./plan"`

**`resolvePlanModelSelection` status:**
Model resolution moves into `planInteractiveOp.model`. `resolvePlanModelSelection` no longer needs to be called in `planCommand()`. The function remains in `plan-runtime.ts` (exported for backward compat) but remove the call in `plan.ts`.

**Scope**
In: `src/cli/plan.ts`, `src/operations/index.ts`.
Out: No changes to `src/cli/plan-runtime.ts` internals, `src/debate/`, or pipeline stages.
